WEBVTT

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:06.490
Sawatari and Gongenzaka ended up 
fighting the Xyz Dimension duelist Kaito.

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.120
Before Academia's invasion,

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.920
Kaito was Ute and Kurosaki's rival 
at their local duel school.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.520
It was said he was strong enough to one day 
become Heartland's duel champion.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:24.170
Now, anger is all that's there.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:25.870
Anger?

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.340
Are you ready to make your confession?

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:31.810
Annihilating Cipher Stream!

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:43.340
Gongenzaka...

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:44.290
Sawatari!

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:45.390
You won't escape, either!

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:50.040
You'll become a card with those two.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.330
The Aquaria Project.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:01:00.110
In their plan to create an ideal world, 
the Fusion Dimension's Academia

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:05.340
has driven Heartland City, in the Xyz 
Dimension, to the brink of obliteration.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:44.010
The Heartless Hunter

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.950
I won't let anyone else be turned into a card!

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.120
Not Sawatari. Not Gongenzaka.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.420
Not the Heartland survivors.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.360
Not the Academia soldiers!

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.700
It's no use.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.620
Right now, Kaito's in no mood to listen.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:02.330
Whether or not he'll listen, 
I'll reach him with a duel.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.300
I learned in City, during my duel with Jack,

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:10.200
that if I put my words, my thoughts, into a duel...

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.940
Kaito and I can reach an understanding!

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:17.710
If you know my name, then you 
must be from Academia.

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:20.280
No! I'm not with Academia!

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:24.860
I know that Academia's squads 
have been ordered to kill me.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:29.610
Because I've turned so many 
of their soldiers into cards.

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.170
It's only natural.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:36.190
But you people have transformed 
many dozens more!

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.570
But I made a vow.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:43.100
For every hundred of my comrades 
you turn into cards,

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:46.400
I will turn a thousand from Academia.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.980
Soon, you'll be one of them!

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:52.340
Are you ready to make your confession?!

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:56.550
I just want to communicate 
with you... Using a duel!

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.420
Field Spell Crossover.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.240
I will not communicate!

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.150
Academia must fall!

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.100
Duel!

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.100
I'll go first!

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.670
I summon Cipher Wing from my hand!

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:17.770
When there's a Cipher Wing 
on my side of the field,

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:21.560
I can Special Summon another 
Cipher Wing from my hand!

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:26.310
Two Cipher Wings again!

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:30.780
And I activate my Continuous Spell 
Double Exposure from my hand,

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:34.200
to double the levels of both Cipher Wings!

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:37.630
Here it comes!

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:38.860
Not good...

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:43.930
I Overlay two Level 8 Cipher Wings!

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:51.680
Galaxy shining in the darkness...

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:55.610
Dwell within the god of vengeance 
and become my servant!

00:04:58.210 --> 00:04:59.680
Xyz Summon!

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:05.620
Descend, Rank 8 Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.380
Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon...

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:13.120
He brought out his ace monster on the first turn.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:18.040
I set one card and end my turn.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:20.060
Yuya...

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:24.110
True, you were able to use your duel 
to communicate with Jack Atlas.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:28.310
That thrill was enough to reach 
even me, inside of you.

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:33.280
But that was only possible because you 
and Jack wanted the same thing.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:34.950
The same thing?

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:38.750
Both you and Jack wished to 
bring peace to that world.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.680
But right now, Kaito is a slave to his anger.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:44.920
He'll bare his fangs to anyone he encounters.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.460
Like an injured beast.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:48.010
You can't communicate with him.

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:48.920
I can!

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.200
I believe that!

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.430
I think you believe it, too.

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.600
Because that time...

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.540
Make people smile by dueling.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:04.020
Use your power to bring smiles

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:08.180
to the world and the future.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:12.330
If he's from the Xyz Dimension like you,

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.700
he must want peace, too.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.590
My turn!

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:22.400
I set the Pendulum Scale with 
Scale 2 Timebreaker Magician

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.540
and Scale 4 Performapal Whim Witch!

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:39.080
And I activate Timebreaker 
Magician's Pendulum Effect

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.880
to double Whim Witch's scale.

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:49.950
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 3 and 7 simultaneously!

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.890
Swing, my soul's pendulum.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:56.830
Draw a shining arc in the sky!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.460
Pendulum Summon!

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:01.610
Appear, my monsters!

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:06.170
First, Performapal Drummerilla!

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:11.400
Then, come out, the heroic one with 
beautiful different-colored eyes,

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:13.800
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:21.100
Battle! Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon 
attacks Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:24.790
In that instant, Drummerilla's 
monster effect activates!

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:29.020
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon's 
attack points increase by 600!

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:33.430
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon's attack points 
are higher than those of Galaxy-Eyes!

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:35.210
Great one, Yuya...

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:38.260
Charge forward and crush that dragon!

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:40.520
This is how I duel.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.110
These are my words!

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:45.440
Putting my feelings into one 
strike! Go, Odd-Eyes!

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:47.320
Spiral Strike—

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:52.750
Continuous Trap Double Exposure lets 
me choose one monster per turn,

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:56.570
and give it the same name as another 
controlled by the same duelist.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:02.040
I choose Drummerilla and name it 
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:08:04.660 --> 00:08:06.240
Two Odd-Eyes Dragons?

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:07.570
What's he planning?

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.770
I activate my trap Double Sensorship!

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:17.440
Once per turn, if a monster on the field 
shares a name with the one battling,

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:19.280
I negate the attack!

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:28.450
He doubled Odd-Eyes so he could use that trap.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:34.010
In that instant, Drummerilla's effect ends,

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:36.690
and Odd-Eyes's attack points 
return to normal.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:44.040
And Timebreaker Magician's 
Pendulum Effect also ends,

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:46.710
returning Whim Witch's scale to normal.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:49.970
I end my turn.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:52.410
He used Pendulum to call up Odd-Eyes,

00:08:52.410 --> 00:08:56.590
increased its attack points with the 
Drummerilla activated at the same time,

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:57.960
and then did battle.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.420
Yuya's strategy had no flaws.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:03.820
Yet it ended with him being 
unable to do anything.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:05.610
Not bad at all.

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:11.160
Of course, he was strong enough to beat me back, so I suppose it's only natural...

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:15.170
Your misfortune is that you 
fought me after they did.

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:16.110
What?

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:19.770
Once I see an enemy's moves, 
I never forget them.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:24.060
Pendulum Summon lets you summon 
multiple monsters at once.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:28.000
And using them in attack combos 
is your primary strategy.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.380
In the fight with the other two, I learned that.

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:33.050
Dealing with an opponent is easy,

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:35.980
once you understand his strategy and tactics.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.860
As I did just now.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:41.960
Sorry, Yuya! If only I hadn't failed!

00:09:42.530 --> 00:09:45.660
I have seen through your means of dueling.

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:48.930
So now, you cannot beat me!

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:51.880
My turn.

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:56.340
I use one Overlay Unit on 
Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:58.220
to activate its monster effect!

00:09:58.220 --> 00:10:00.140
Cipher Projection!

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:06.890
Once per turn, I can take control of one 
monster on your side of the field,

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.520
with its effect negated.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:11.660
I take control of Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon,

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:15.140
and treat it as a Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:20.230
Odd-Eyes...

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:25.320
And I activate my Continuous Spell 
Cipher Interference from my hand!

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:27.770
Battle!

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:32.830
I attack the Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon 
that was once Drummerilla

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:34.710
with Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:40.890
He wants Yuya's monsters 
to take each other out.

00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:44.490
In that instant, I activate 
Drummerilla's monster effect!

00:10:44.840 --> 00:10:48.940
Until the Battle Phase ends, its attack 
points increase by 600!

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:54.930
You can reduce the damage you 
take in this battle that way, but...

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:56.910
Your struggles are useless.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:11:00.000
Since there are two Cipher 
Dragons on the field,

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.720
Continuous Spell Cipher Interference's effect

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:05.580
doubles the attack points of the one in battle!

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:12.880
Go, Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:15.140
You won't get me that easily!

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.930
Annihilating Cipher Stream!

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:23.540
I activate my Action Spell Miracle!

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:28.810
I negate my monster's destruction by battle, 
and halve the damage I take!

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:30.470
Yuya!

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:37.210
So not only can Action Cards be used 
to attack, but to defend, as well?

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:39.470
No, not only those...

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:44.060
They can also increase monster 
effects, recover life, and lots—

00:11:44.060 --> 00:11:45.470
I don't require your explanation.

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:48.160
I will destroy all of you with my duel.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:50.060
Miracle can only be used once!

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:56.180
Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon attacks 
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:11:57.100 --> 00:11:58.160
Now...

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:00.670
Annihilating Cipher Stream!

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:13.280
When battle ends, so does 
Cipher Interference's effect.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:18.360
I set one card and end my turn.

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:24.450
In that instant, control of Odd-Eyes 
Pendulum Dragon,

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:28.930
which I usurped with Galaxy-Eyes Cipher 
Dragon's effect, returns to you.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:33.900
But I'll destroy it soon, too!

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.070
And when I do, you're finished!

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:45.970
He's strong.

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:47.830
Overwhelmingly strong.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:52.630
But his ability to precisely read my 
tactics is even more amazing.

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:55.150
You were right, Ute.

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:59.210
And it seems that ability is 
even sharper than it was.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:03.530
I sense the readiness to cut down anything, 
the second it gets close.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:07.130
As he is right now, he won't listen to you.

00:13:07.130 --> 00:13:12.340
That's why I'll use my duel to 
get through to his heart!

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:13.850
My turn!

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:16.540
It's here.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:19.510
Has Yuya found a new strategy?

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:24.590
I activate the Pendulum Effect of Whim 
Witch, which is already set.

00:13:24.590 --> 00:13:27.950
I Special Summon it from my 
Pendulum Zone to my field.

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:32.420
Then, I activate Whim Witch's monster effect!

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:36.670
When it's used as a component 
in a Tribute Summon,

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:38.170
it counts as two monsters!

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:41.030
I tribute Whim Witch,

00:13:41.360 --> 00:13:44.500
to Tribute Summon Dragoncaller 
Magician from my hand!

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.810
Dragoncaller Magician's monster effect.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:58.450
Once per turn, until my End Phase,

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:02.490
I can switch its type from Spellcaster to Dragon!

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:09.380
Now, you have two Level 7 dragons.

00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:13.080
Watch, Ute...

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:16.400
With my strongest monster 
and my ultimate duel,

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:18.340
I'll pry open Kaito's heart!

00:14:20.350 --> 00:14:26.330
I overlay Level 7 Odd-Eyes Pendulum 
Dragon and Dragoncaller Magician!

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:34.550
Dragon with different-colored eyes,

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:39.720
exterminate your enemies with your black wrath!

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:41.390
Xyz Summon!

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:44.330
Come out, Rank 7...

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:46.590
With shining eyes of fury!

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:50.280
Odd-Eyes Rebellion Dragon!

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:55.530
A new dragon... And he Xyz Summoned it?

00:14:55.530 --> 00:14:57.420
Who is this man?

00:14:58.140 --> 00:14:58.990
Battle!

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:03.810
Odd-Eyes Rebellion Dragon attacks 
Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:11.040
But Yuya's and his dragons both 
have 3000 attack points.

00:15:11.040 --> 00:15:12.490
Is he going for a tie?

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:13.830
No...

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:16.670
If a monster that used Dragoncaller 
Magician as a component

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:18.960
battles another Dragon-Type Monster,

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:21.240
its attack points are doubled!

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:28.320
Yes!

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:29.850
Now, he can win.

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.910
He can avenge us, too!

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:35.720
I activate my set card Double Cipher.

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:41.270
I use all remaining Overlay Units on 
my Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon,

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:45.210
to Special Summon another 
Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:48.620
from my Extra Deck, ignoring its 
summon requirements!

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:55.510
Galaxy shining in the darkness...

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:59.700
Dwell within the god of vengeance 
and become my servant!

00:16:01.910 --> 00:16:03.370
Xyz Summon!

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:09.640
Descend, Rank 8 Galaxy-Eyes Cipher Dragon!

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:15.960
In that instant, the effect of the currently active 
Continuous Spell Cipher Interference

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:19.660
doubles Galaxy-Eyes Cipher 
Dragon's attack points!

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:21.530
What?!

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:22.610
Incredible.

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:26.300
He's using Cipher Interference 
for defense, as well?

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:30.000
Then, his dragon has 6000 
attack points, too.

00:16:48.710 --> 00:16:52.250
Dark-Eyes Rebellion was 
Yuya's strongest monster.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:56.830
Incredible. And he still has 
another dragon left...

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:59.560
There's no way Yuya can win now.

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:07.240
S-Still not enough? How do I find Kaito's heart?

00:17:07.810 --> 00:17:09.980
Rebellion Dragon's monster effect!

00:17:11.180 --> 00:17:14.780
Do it! This is your only chance to use it!

00:17:15.700 --> 00:17:18.920
I activate Odd-Eyes Rebellion 
Dragon's monster effect!

00:17:18.920 --> 00:17:21.250
When this card leaves the field,

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:24.250
I can destroy all cards in my 
Pendulum Zones

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:28.440
and set Odd-Eyes Rebellion Dragon there!

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:33.960
Then I activate Odd-Eyes Rebellion 
Dragon's Pendulum Effect!

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:38.620
I can set one card from my deck 
in the open Pendulum Zone.

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:46.310
I choose Scale 1 Performapal Lebellman, 
and set the Pendulum Scale with it.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:57.860
Now I can summon monsters between 
Levels 2 and 3 simultaneously!

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:00.590
Pendulum Summon!

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:03.420
Appear, my monsters!

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:09.000
Be reborn from my Extra Deck, 
Timebreaker Magician!

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:12.040
And Performapal Whim Witch!

00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:15.020
Two Level 3 monsters...

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:17.710
Is he going to Xyz Summon again?

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:22.200
There's no trace of Kaito's old warmth in his duel.

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.630
It's full of rage.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:28.440
I've fought this far, hoping to 
quell that rage just a little.

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:30.920
Kaito's heart is closed.

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:34.600
Ute... You were right.

00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:38.250
Maybe I only succeeded in City 
because I was fighting Jack.

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:41.510
No... I knew that.

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:45.700
My power alone still isn't enough 
to make everyone smile.

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:48.250
I'm powerless, too.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:53.030
Using the power we have now, 
how can we open Kaito's heart?

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:59.880
What strategy should we use to open 
his heart's tightly closed door?

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:00.820
Ute...

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:04.060
And here's the answer we found!

00:19:04.060 --> 00:19:04.860
I...

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:08.830
...activate Performapal Lebellman's 
Pendulum Effect!

00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:14.230
Once per turn, I can increase the level 
of all monsters on my field by 1.

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:21.000
Then, I...

00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:26.260
...overlay Level 4 Timebreaker Magician 
and Performapal Whim Witch!

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:34.020
From the black darkness,

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:38.940
the fangs of rebellion that fight against 
the powers of stupidity descend!

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:41.660
Xyz Summon!

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:47.140
Appear, Rank 4 Dark Rebellion Xyz Dragon!

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:52.070
Th-This is... Can it be...

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:55.310
Yes! It's me, Kaito!

00:19:56.130 --> 00:20:00.840
Seeing my ace monster, Dark Rebellion 
Xyz Dragon, you must remember...

00:20:01.890 --> 00:20:06.240
You can't have forgotten all those 
times you fought Syun and me,

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:07.990
back at the duel academy!

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:11.520
Wh-Why? Why do you have that monster?

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:13.500
Did you steal it?

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:17.430
Did you defeat Ute and take that monster?

00:20:20.220 --> 00:20:21.240
Are you...

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:23.370
Can you be... Ute?

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:28.220
That's Yuya.

00:20:29.810 --> 00:20:31.510
He's with me.

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:33.980
Syun?

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:35.210
Kurosaki?

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:36.860
That's right, Kaito.

00:20:36.860 --> 00:20:40.030
Syun returned with new allies.

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:41.870
Three of them.

00:20:41.870 --> 00:20:45.690
Even one would be valuable, 
so it's nice to see.

00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:46.970
Allies?

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.450
You doubt me?

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:56.920
Don't worry.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.570
He hates the dimensional war 
from the bottom of his heart.

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.770
He wants to stop Academia's tyranny.

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:06.460
I confirmed it during my fight 
in the Synchro Dimension.

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:08.010
Synchro Dimension?

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:10.190
Trust in me, Kaito.

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:12.580
And Yuya Sakaki, whom I trust.

00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:14.320
Sakaki?

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.620
Kaito, come back with us.

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:19.280
And fight with us again—

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:20.020
No!

00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:23.260
I already severed my ties to you!

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:46.680
Kaito...

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:55.480
Kaito disappeared?

00:21:58.900 --> 00:21:59.830
Kaito...

00:23:52.040 --> 00:23:55.380
Of all places, I've been sent 
to the Fusion Dimension?

00:23:55.380 --> 00:23:57.920
And why are they chasing me?

00:23:57.920 --> 00:24:01.490
You can't escape! Just turn 
yourself in, peacefully!

00:24:01.490 --> 00:24:04.280
If they take me, I'll be sent to Academia.

00:24:04.280 --> 00:24:06.680
That's what the Professor wants!

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:09.100
I'll just have to fight...

00:24:09.100 --> 00:24:11.830
Hold it! I'll fight you!

00:24:12.630 --> 00:24:16.680
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Spectacular Cyber Angels.

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:18.630
The fun is only getting started!
